E=[('Read-aloud · an undefined churchy word', 107, 'But love in the real world runs into a wall the catechumens of every age have had to face:', 'But love in the real world runs into a wall every Christian in every age has had to face:'), ('Read-aloud · dash spacing', 130, 'This is a truth reason can glimpse—the Church teaches that human dignity "is fully recognizable even by reason alone" (*Dignitas Infinita*, 1)—yet whole', 'This is a truth reason can glimpse — the Church teaches that human dignity "is fully recognizable even by reason alone" (*Dignitas Infinita*, 1) — yet whole'), ('Read-aloud · hard to say', 138, 'it is love trying to be born by un-loving, and the act simply cancels itself.', 'it tries to bring about love by refusing to love, and the act cancels itself.'), ('Read-aloud · hard to say', 152, 'a noise to be switched off to purchase survivals.', 'a noise to be silenced so that others may survive.'), ('Read-aloud · sentence order', 154, 'drawing their attention in hopes of saving the others and the baby. Love may lay down its own life for another; it may never take an innocent life, its own included. That offering or risking would be the greatest love there is. But you cannot offer or risk what is not yours.', 'drawing their attention in hopes of saving the others and the baby. That offering or risking would be the greatest love there is. Love may lay down its own life for another; it may never take an innocent life, its own included. You cannot offer or risk what is not yours.'), ('Read-aloud · hard to say', 156, "to the God who Himself drew the salvation of the world out of an innocent man's murder He did not prevent but redeemed.", 'to the God who drew the salvation of the world out of the murder of His own innocent Son, a death He did not prevent but redeemed.'), ('Banned framing · paid in full', 210, 'On the Cross, mercy did not bypass justice — it flowed *through* a justice that had been paid in full by Christ, so that', 'On the Cross, mercy did not bypass justice — it flowed *through* justice, as Christ offered Himself in love for our sins, so that'), ('Banned framing · debt', 212, 'a mercy that merely pronounces a debt forgiven from across the room has not yet become love.', 'a mercy that merely pronounces the sin forgiven from across the room has not yet become love.'), ('Banned word · checklist', 274, 'is the work of a lifetime, not a checklist.', 'is the work of a lifetime, not a list of rules.')]
